#
# LF in every working tree, whatever the machine's core.autocrlf says. Git for
# Windows installs with autocrlf=true system-wide, and a CRLF checkout breaks
# every line-anchored parser in this repository: on the first Windows CI run
# about 300 vitest cases failed on carriage returns alone (the UI register read
# as empty, the workflow guards could not find their own jobs). text=auto
# leaves binary files (the golden PDFs, images) untouched.
* text=auto eol=lf
# Documents are bytes: a PDF without NUL bytes still reads as text to git, and
# its xref offsets die with the first converted line ending.
*.pdf binary
